<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="23120274 - Stress - Category Management &amp; Verification" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">[DESIGN ONLY; NOT EXECUTED] Created 2026-11-19 Asia/Saigon.
Five concurrent native cohorts, 10 threads each; ramps20s, delays0/80/160/240/320s, durations400/320/240/160/80s. Nominal stable levels10/20/30/40/50 each60s, total400s main+60s quiet recovery+setup/cleanup. Closed workload; RPS measured, no SLA invented. No plugin.
Load evidence:5595 HTTP samples,1119 each label,0 failed,cleanup VERIFIED; not a capacity proof. i5-11400H6cores12logical/16123MiB; freeRAM1335MiB at2026-11-19 15:54:19+07 below2048MiB floor. Future execution blocked until memory recovered and approvals renewed. Load observed backend working set max101.676MiB, machine-normalized CPU max4.12%, freeRAM min2464MiB; these are not stress capacity predictions.
Same CSV/hash, five HTTPs, JSON correlation, ownership contracts and1000-2000ms think once before Login. One reusable workflow fragment referenced by five Module Controllers. Cohort-local initializer maps workers1..50; token and categoryID remain thread-local.
Stress adapter reuses unchanged Load helper and recovery. Default approval flags false:hw05.allow_mutation,hw05.isolated_sut,hw05.stress_reviewed. Credentials ENV only ESHOP_ADMIN_EMAIL/ESHOP_ADMIN_PASSWORD. Configurable csv_file/project_root/host/port/timeouts; target localhost only; min_free_mib&gt;=2048. Fixed cohort schedule cannot be changed with load_threads/ramp_seconds/duration_seconds. Think properties must stay1000/1000.
Performance availability errors429/500/502/503/504 or allowlisted transport failures at Login/View before intent are FAILED samples; dependencies skipped, paced next iteration allowed. No retry of Create/Delete. All identity/account/contract/manifest/baseline errors and uncertain mutations set global safety abort: no new iterations/intents, confirmed owned records can finish cleanup. Latency alone does not trigger invented duration assertions.
Create intent force-to-storage before request; confirmed actual ID before Delete, exclude baseline/product refs, verify absence by ID and exact name. Isolated SUT/no actors/no backend restart required. No extra guard GET inside measured five-step workflow. Create read-after-write proof remains pilot/out-of-window verification.
Aggregate Report main HTTP only, no configured output filename; do not retain bodies/headers/secrets. Setup/controls/tearDown ignored. Recovery quiet60s is not proof of no late writes. Guarded reconciliation outside measurement uses unchanged recovery script; unknown outcome remains unresolved absent explicit quiescence acknowledgment. Forced kill can skip teardown. Independent recovery --apply additionally requires --isolated --quiescent, credentials and source/baseline checks. No prefix deletion/reset.
No Stress launcher/pilot/run created or performed. Existing Load launcher/checker remain Load-specific and must not execute this plan. Stress execution needs separate approval/preflight and resource monitoring; static validation cannot prove scheduling, runtime cleanup or capacity.

Execution preparation 2026-11-19: default official schedule unchanged. Explicit stress_mode=pilot requires all validated pilot properties: 5 cohorts x1VU, ramp1s, delays0/3/6/9/12s, durations30/27/24/21/18s, quiet recovery60s, same think time. Pilot results must be separate. All profile properties validated before Login. Use Stress launcher only; default PrepareOnly.

Dashboard requires responseMessage: Stress assertions replace it with an allowlisted diagnostic code before listeners; no raw server/transport message retained. HTTP status and success remain actual measured values.
</stringProp>
